@@ -0,0 +1,36 @@
+# Generated RPC route-count proof (diagnostic only)
+
+This standalone friend-assembly executable uses the exact `IStreamLoadService` and
+`StreamLoadService` declarations copied from `SharpLink.StreamLoadTest/Program.cs`.
+The normal generator emits its proxy and server stub; the normal client/server
+builders run them over a paired in-memory `System.IO.Pipelines` transport. No OS
+socket or named/anonymous OS pipe is opened by the probe.
+
+Activate the repository's normal .NET SDK, then run `./test/SharpLink.RouteCountProbe/run-proof.sh`.
+The script builds once and runs three fresh processes per OFF/ON mode, preserving
+JSON results, stderr, build output, and before/after DLL hashes in `evidence/`.
+`SHARPLINK_DIAGNOSTIC_QUIESCENT=0|1` is read by the existing module-initialized adapter.
+
+Each process performs, in order:
+
+1. Connect and capture a baseline.
+2. 8 warmup and 64 measured `AddAsync(7, 9)` calls, each returning 16, before any stream.
+3. 8 warmup and 64 measured `DownloadAsync(1)` calls, each yielding exactly `[0]`.
+4. One separately reported generated unary fence after streaming, then a pre-teardown snapshot.
+5. Client/server disposal and a separate teardown snapshot, including framework-task drain checks.
+
+Counters cover all core `CompleteStream` entries (before lookup), null-map/miss
+classification, actual helper entry, successful fast claim/completion, registration,
+DATA dispatch, both request-retirement entry points, and `CompleteAll` separately.
+Every side has an explicit zero-filled counter schema. Wire-frame counts are separate.
+The snapshots include live route/pending-call counts, all captured entry retirement
+states, pool count, and selected RPC reference/token cleanup checks.
+
+The repository's `HasRetainedReferencesForTests` includes `_current is not null`,
+which is always true for `int`; the probe therefore checks its reference/token
+fields directly. It does not alter the existing predicate or any shipping cleanup.
+Diagnostic captures intentionally retain entry objects, so this is not a GC-retention
+or allocation test. These counter additions must never enter a timing binary.
+In-memory transport counts establish routing, not performance equivalence to TCP,
+UDS, shared memory, or any other transport. Healthy successful RPCs are tested;
+error-cleanup call sites are documented separately, not exercised by failure injection.
